      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Dc susceptibility (2–300 K, 1000 Oe) shows χMT = 18.39 cm3 K mol−1 at 300 K (calc. 18.75 for uncoupled Gd3+ and Mn3+), remaining nearly constant then dropping rapidly from 50 K to 13.75 cm3 K mol−1 at 4 K, indicating antiferromagnetic coupling. Curie–Weiss C = 18.72 cm3 K mol−1 with a negative Weiss constant. Magnetization at 7 T is 16.06 NμB versus a theoretical saturation of 18.00 NμB.",
