        "summary": "χMT = 52.28 cm3 K mol−1 at 300 K (calc. 52.89), nearly constant until 30 K then falling to 21.22 cm3 K mol−1 at 2 K, indicating dominant antiferromagnetism. Curie–Weiss C = 52.94 cm3 K mol−1 with a negative Weiss constant. QMC fit of 3: J1 = −0.401(5) cm−1, J2 = 0.370(7) cm−1 (Gd–Mn); J3 = −0.498(7) cm−1, J4 = 0.711(7) cm−1 (Gd–Gd); D1 = 0.000 cm−1, D2 = 2.924(1) cm−1, g = 1.998, zJ = −0.030 cm−1, R = 2.128×10−5. Mixed ferro/antiferromagnetic couplings, with AF Gd–Mn and Gd–Gd dominant at low T. M(7 T) = 22.12 NμB vs theoretical 50.00 NμB.",
